The article discusses the historical pneumatic tube system used for underground mail delivery in the United States from 1893 to 1953, where mail traveled at speeds of 35 MPH. It also references Senator Ted Stevens' controversial analogy of the internet as 'a series of tubes,' which was ridiculed but has roots in this earlier technology.

